      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T19:15:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi, happy to help fixing the treehugger issue.\n\nFirst, I want to confirm the intended behaviour when `ACTION_DEVICE_CUSTOMIZATION_READY` is triggered (I don\u0027t have any context about this intent):\n\nIn the previous version: if no custom wallpaper has been set, set the wallpaper to be an ImageWallpaper with the default drawable.\n\nIn the new version: if the WallpaperService is an ImageWallpaper, restart the WallpaperService (without changing the bitmap it\u0027s using).\n\nCan you confirm that this is the expected behaviour? Also could you explain what is the `ACTION_DEVICE_CUSTOMIZATION_READY` intent, and why ImageWallpaper needs to be restarted (but not live wallpapers)?\n\nThanks!",
      "revId": "a71fb1062fccfcd5c9dd2f7d6cfc9b4c55203565",
